{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7657","id":5210882295,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNpfA9w","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7657","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7657.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7657.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7657","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7657/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7657/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7657/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/9650bf71975805e0d196741adefe035f8a90f2a2","number":7657,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(id): generic event-body persistence, retrieval and range-sync (#4837)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #4837\n\nGeneric event-body persistence for `pkgs/id`'s event store — the prerequisite the didit tracker phases (#2031) were missing: `store_event` persisted headers only, ingest verified bodies against the header and dropped them, and range sync carried no bodies.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Storage** (`event_store/mod.rs`): new `bodies` table (event ID → body bytes); store format bumped to `id.events.store.v9` (previous-format stores are refused and keep their data, as with prior bumps — covered by the existing format test).\n- **Ingest** (`event_store/ingest.rs`): the verified body from `ingest_with_body` is threaded through `ingest_event`/`ingest_in`/`settle` and stored when its event is accepted, held, or parked; a body arriving later for a header-only stored event is stored on the duplicate path (and counts as a change, so the transaction commits). New `ingest_events_with_bodies` batch entry point verifies every body against its signed header (BLAKE3 hash + size) before storing — a non-committed body refuses its event in place and stores nothing.\n- **Retrieval**: `EventStore::event_body(id)` returns the body byte-identically, or the new typed `StoreError::MissingBody` when the event is header-only, its body never arrived, or the ID is unknown. Header-only events are otherwise unaffected.\n- **Range sync** (`event_store/sync.rs`, `store_traits.rs`): data-phase records now carry the body after the event bytes (length-prefixed by the event length); the receiver checks the body against the header commitment before ingest and stores it through the batch path. The now-unused body-less `RangeStore::ingest_events` shim was removed.\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test --lib event_store` in `pkgs/id`: **134 passed, 0 failed** (was 133 + this change's new tests net +5, one pre-existing test adapted to the batch tuple shape).\n\nNew tests:\n- body stored at ingest and read back byte-identically\n- missing body is the typed `MissingBody` not-found (stored header-only and unknown ID)\n- body arriving after its header is stored on the duplicate path\n- a batch body that is not the committed one refuses its event; the committed body is stored\n- range sync carries bodies: a loopback session delivers bodies to the peer store, read back byte-identically\n\nQueue task 13568 (lane code-w).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796728906&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7657&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7657&signature=ec210a3d1fb793fffffbdf4dd5d253728f0d5da8f481838789dbda8cddeec600\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7657?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T11:21:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-13T09:47:10Z","closed_at":"2026-11-13T09:47:07Z","merged_at":"2026-11-13T09:47:07Z","merge_commit_sha":"d18dd194488aab3e36bea90ef54aaec62d5cacc6","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/